{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786593755748429002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"cryptic-damp-panda","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"de4bce62384e979bad60b7486e45b703b9677d6280b224074b822dd41eed55cb","event_uuid":"58248bb3-e4d1-4bbf-a436-5fc97c3ab4a0","position":{"commit_sha":"b59ca59bfe3e5e35b7d73371ff6ea6d16fb04e15","position":"1786593745257672001-58248bb3-e4d1-4bbf-a436-5fc97c3ab4a0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e01c7462c419a75d9ee25c4154e0a1c299bf0e9c91f4b833b0ae7af0c2120136","event_uuid":"771f203b-d1fe-494d-8999-382b384a836e","position":{"commit_sha":"eb137a576d68183e8afbd8be32d8daa7c9f064ff","position":"1786593755062109001-771f203b-d1fe-494d-8999-382b384a836e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0a9c75129b0efed8ccef00046936f511d3a20d0208d7336dcfef17b88dd5e705","event_uuid":"253ecb59-75a2-469d-8453-1dcdf606de98","position":{"commit_sha":"eb137a576d68183e8afbd8be32d8daa7c9f064ff","position":"1786593755748429001-253ecb59-75a2-469d-8453-1dcdf606de98"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786593745257672001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context\nGerrit Verified on GitHub Actions is now frequently 30–40 minutes, roughly double the prior 15–20 minute duration. The recent mutation-testing addition is a lead, not a conclusion. Prior work on baseborn-subtle-cricket, crushable-choosable-llama, and coercive-paediatric-bug measured earlier critical paths and org-wide runner contention; this investigation must distinguish execution time from queue time and must not re-propose rejected runner parallelism that leaves total runner usage unchanged.\n\n## Plan\n- Build a dated evidence dossier from current and historical gerrit-verify runs, job and step timings, workflow history, and the prior CI-latency tickets.\n- Identify the good-to-bad transition and quantify mutation testing contribution using comparable runs or a controlled local/CI experiment.\n- Generate falsifiable rival hypotheses and run discriminating experiments, including runtime evidence for dynamic causes.\n- Record a cited root cause and reference existing tickets for every remediation to prove whether it is new, accepted, completed, or previously rejected.\n- If existing telemetry is insufficient, add the smallest assurance-neutral observability needed, validate it, and land it through Gerrit before concluding.\n- Propose wall-clock reductions that preserve coverage and do not rely on increasing parallel jobs or unchanged aggregate runner consumption.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The current 30–40 minute symptom is decomposed into workflow queue time, job queue time, and execution critical path across a representative run sample.\n- [ ] The good-to-bad transition is identified with dated workflow or commit evidence.\n- [ ] Mutation testing has a specific measured wall-clock and runner-time contribution, including comparable before and after evidence.\n- [ ] Rival hypotheses are confirmed or rejected by falsifiable experiments, with dynamic claims supported by runtime evidence.\n- [ ] The proven root cause is recorded with repository, run, and ticket citations.\n- [ ] Every proposed remediation references searched tracker history and states whether it is new, completed, accepted, or previously rejected.\n- [ ] Recommendations preserve CI coverage and avoid parallelism that does not reduce aggregate runner usage.\n- [ ] Any required observability change passes repository gates, Gerrit LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and is merged before this ticket closes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"771f203b-d1fe-494d-8999-382b384a836e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","gerrit","debug"],"ticket_id":"ba7d-a412-bbc0-45cb","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Root-cause current Gerrit Verified CI latency regression and quantify mutation testing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["58248bb3-e4d1-4bbf-a436-5fc97c3ab4a0","771f203b-d1fe-494d-8999-382b384a836e","253ecb59-75a2-469d-8453-1dcdf606de98"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786593755748429002,"uuid":"5a5180d9-4e79-4a07-aae6-8a8ad634581b"}